Use alloc, core.

Let i be 0.
While i is less than 60.
Let p be allocate 32 bytes.
Set p[0] to 7.
Release memory at p.
Add 1 to i.
End the loop.
Let p be allocate 1 bytes.
Release memory at p.
Set p to no address.
Release memory at p.
Let empty block be allocate 0 bytes.
Release memory at empty block.
Let used be bytes in use.
If used is not 0.
Stop with error "churn leak".
End the condition.
Give back 0.
